From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 1 Sep 2026 18:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] user_manager: never let adb failure abort userUnlocked

userUnlocked() is the reply to a binder call the container makes from
system_server's UserController thread. 1.4.2 calls adb_connect() there
unguarded, and adb_connect() raises RuntimeError whenever "adb start-server"
fails - trivially easy on a device where adb has no writable HOME:

  RuntimeError: Command failed: % adb start-server

The exception escapes the callback, so the reply never comes, the container's
UserController thread stays blocked, and sixty seconds later Android's own
watchdog kills system_server:

  Watchdog: at lineageos.waydroid.UserMonitor.userUnlocked(UserMonitor.java:81)
  Watchdog: at org.lineageos.platform.internal.WayDroidService.onUnlockUser
  Watchdog: at com.android.server.SystemServiceManager.unlockUser
  Watchdog: *** GOODBYE!

Android restarts, unlocks the user, calls again and loops. On mindphone that
presented as a UI stuck on "system is starting" with SystemUI unresponsive,
processes climbing from 75 to 105 over six minutes as each generation's
SystemUI and launcher were orphaned, and sys.boot_completed=1 the whole time -
so nothing in "waydroid status" showed it.

The app list sync immediately below never ran either, which is why no launcher
entries ever appeared.

1.6.3 both guards this call and makes it conditional on auto_adb, which 1.6.0
turned off by default. Guarding is the half that matters here; leaving the
call unconditional keeps existing behaviour where adb does work.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [fixed differently upstream in 1.6.3]
---
--- a/tools/services/user_manager.py
+++ b/tools/services/user_manager.py
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 import os
 import threading
 import tools.config
+from contextlib import suppress
 import tools.helpers.net
 from tools.interfaces import IUserMonitor
 from tools.interfaces import IPlatform
@@ -66,7 +67,25 @@
     def userUnlocked(uid):
         logging.info("Android with user {} is ready".format(uid))
 
-        tools.helpers.net.adb_connect(args)
+        # Never let this abort the callback. userUnlocked() is the reply to a
+        # binder call the container makes from system_server's UserController
+        # thread; an exception here means that reply never comes, the thread
+        # stays blocked, and sixty seconds later Android's own watchdog kills
+        # system_server:
+        #
+        #   Watchdog: at lineageos.waydroid.UserMonitor.userUnlocked
+        #   Watchdog: at ...WayDroidService.onUnlockUser
+        #   Watchdog: *** GOODBYE!
+        #
+        # Android then restarts, unlocks the user, calls again, and loops -
+        # leaving the UI stuck on "system is starting" with orphaned SystemUI
+        # processes piling up from each generation.
+        #
+        # adb_connect() raises RuntimeError whenever "adb start-server" fails,
+        # which is easy on a device where adb has no writable HOME. Worse, the
+        # app list sync below never runs, so launcher entries never appear.
+        with suppress(RuntimeError):
+            tools.helpers.net.adb_connect(args)
 
         platformService = IPlatform.get_service(args)
         if platformService:
